      <title>COP31: Do We Really Need 92,000 People at a Climate Conference?</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-11-19/cop31-do-we-really-need-92-000-people-at-a-climate-conference</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">a4902d1f33258b2ea8d9ff48</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:30:02 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>A grand total of 55 delegates attended the US Constitutional Convention in 1787. An even smaller number of rebels met with England’s King John to bang out the Magna Carta in 1215. The point is that sometimes a relative handful of people can resolve big, knotty conflicts with novel, world-changing solutions.</description>
