      <guid isPermaLink="false">4663e334fa35813a9cace8d9</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:00:02 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>The installation of a new router grounded America for four hours last week, even though 68 others just like it had previously been added to the Federal Aviation Administration’s network without incident. There’s a term for what happened last Friday: They’re called normal accidents — and the best way to protect against them is for managers to respect and empower the people who know the system best.</description>
